# --- apps/api (Render / Netlify Functions / local) ---
# Local monorepo: you can keep one `.env` at the repo root — `npm run dev:api` loads it.
# Optional override: `apps/api/.env` (loaded first; root fills any missing vars).
# Use the Supabase URI you prefer. If `migrate deploy` fails through the pooler, switch this to
# the "Direct connection" string from Project Settings → Database (host db.*.supabase.co:5432).
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/postgres?schema=public"

# Optional — Prisma 7 + pg adapter: set to false if you hit TLS / certificate errors (e.g. P1010).
# DATABASE_SSL_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=false

# Optional — default 8787 locally; Render sets PORT automatically. Not used on Netlify (serverless).
# PORT=8787
#
# Netlify (Base directory apps/api): set DATABASE_URL, CORS_ORIGIN, etc. in the Netlify UI.
# Install command: cd ../.. && npm ci  ·  Build: prisma migrate deploy (see apps/api/netlify.toml).

# Optional — base URL for FAB card art when a printing has no TCGPlayer id (see `resolveFabCardArtUrl`).
# Leave unset or omit; an empty value is ignored (default fabmaster base is used).
# FAB_CARD_IMAGE_BASE_URL=https://storage.googleapis.com/fabmaster/media/images

# Browser origin(s) allowed to call the API directly (comma-separated). Required in production.
# Local development defaults to http://localhost:3000 and http://127.0.0.1:3000.
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://tu-app.vercel.app

# Secret used to sign anonymous guest sessions. Required in production.
# GUEST_TOKEN_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret

# API abuse protection. Defaults: 120 requests/minute and 1 MiB request bodies.
# API_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=120
# API_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=60000
# API_MAX_BODY_BYTES=1048576

# --- Supabase Auth (API: verify access JWT via JWKS) ---
# Set SUPABASE_URL (e.g. https://xxxx.supabase.co) so the API can load JWKS from
# /auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json. Requires JWT signing that exposes JWKS (Supabase dashboard).
# Or set SUPABASE_JWKS_URL to the full JWKS URL.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json
# Issuer defaults to ${SUPABASE_ORIGIN}/auth/v1 — override if needed:
# SUPABASE_JWT_ISSUER=https://xxxx.supabase.co/auth/v1
# Access tokens use audience "authenticated" by default:
# SUPABASE_JWT_AUDIENCE=authenticated

# Co-op WebSocket: local `npm run dev:api` serves HTTP and WS from the same port.
# Set this only when the browser must use a different WS host/port.
# Local default; override this when the API uses another port or host.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COOP_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:8787/coop-ws
# Legacy companion-process fallback (only needed with `npm run realtime:dev` separately):
# COOP_REALTIME_NOTIFY_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010
# COOP_REALTIME_SECRET=shared-secret

# --- apps/web (Vercel / local Next) ---
# Supabase Auth (browser). These two values enable the Sign in button locally.
# Get them from Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# The anon key is public and browser-safe; never put a service-role key in NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
#
# After setting them, restart `npm run dev` because Next.js reads NEXT_PUBLIC_* at startup.
# OAuth and magic-link callback: http://localhost:3000/auth/callback
# Add that URL under Supabase Dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration.
# Enable the Google/Discord providers there if those buttons are used.

# Proxy /api to the API in dev or if you prefer edge rewrites (same-origin fetches).
# API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# Client-visible WebSocket URL (optional).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COOP_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:3010/coop-ws
